VERDICT: FAIL (reported as status blocked).

P1 — The loader repair does not establish validation-before-execution.
`load_image` only returns entry/callee bytecode
(crates/sley-vm/src/host_abi.rs:163-210); `execute_function` still accepts
canonical `LoweringInput`, calls `lower_function`, and executes that result
(crates/sley-vm/src/execute.rs:354-370). Tests decode or execute separately
rather than execute the supplied loaded image
(crates/sley-vm/tests/rw070_host_abi_freeze.rs:500-535,955-1015). Violates
axis 3 and leaves the future seed-absence condition untestable without
adding another execution boundary, contrary to
docs/spec/HOST_ABI_V1.md:112-132.

P1 — Image/profile/import identities are not bound end-to-end. `LoadedImage`
carries no digest, cache key, profile, epoch, root, import manifest, or
limits (host_abi.rs:163-181). The cache key contains profile fields but no
image digest, bootstrap-profile digest, import-manifest identity, or limits
(crates/sley-vm/src/lib.rs:130-214); limits enter the observation separately
(execute.rs:1390-1430). `BootstrapProfileReport` contains only functions and
counts (bootstrap.rs:82-98), so gate admission plus observation identity
provides no encoded association among the gate report, loaded bytes, and
execution. Violates axis 4.

P1 — The PSH1 monomorphization pin cannot represent multiple element types
in one closed inventory. The contract requires each concrete `P-PUSH`
instantiation to declare a closed row (docs/spec/EFFECT_SYSTEM_V1.md:122-139)
while request identities are globally distinct (:164-174). Implementation
assigns every push row the same PSH1 entity identity and resolves only the
first matching row (crates/sley-vm/src/extended.rs:263-323). Therefore a
closure cannot carry, for example, both `PSH1<UInt(8)>` and `PSH1<Unit>`,
despite claiming both and any bootstrap T. Violates axis 2 and axis 7.

P2 — Package digest prose is stale.
machineresearch/sley-2.0/reweave/rw-070.md:36-40 cites `7f651ae9…f0c7`,
while the frozen document and supplied authoritative digest are
`a9c7f70d…08eb38`.

Validation by reviewer: static targeted review of the named contract,
manifest, loader, gate, bridge resolver, tests, amendment A1, and G-10
admission. The required Cargo test and marker checker were NOT run: the
reviewer judged the handoff to authorize read only. Owner supplies the
execution records locally (RW-050/RW-060 precedent).

Blockers: an inventory-bound execution path consuming validated loaded bytes
with expected-identity verification; encoded/carried profile/epoch/root/
import/image associations; distinct identities or another closed mechanism
for simultaneous PSH1 monomorphizations; digest prose correction; execution
authority for the two validation commands.

Disposition: ACCEPTED as a failed round. Repairs owned by the RW-070
package. Delta re-review required before close. Preserved unedited as the
failed round.
